/-!
# The two-central HS cover restriction

For the specified HS central quotient with binary kernel, every two-central
involution lifts involutorily. The actual X=O²(C_K(u)) is perfect and maps onto
the model residual; R=O₂(X) has the specified symplectic-type image and A₅
quotient action. Its noncentral order-four image elements form one orbit.

A central cyclic model root lifts to Z(R). Including the central elements in
the square calculation gives [R,R]=Φ(R)=⟨v⟩, where v is the unique square in
uZ(K). Adjoining Z(K) gives the actual Klein four-group ⟨u⟩Z(K). The residual
centralizes Z(R), and central transfer places Z(K) in X. These statements
construct all four centralizer inputs to the independent normalizer branch.

This completes the two-central local branch. The parent HS covering argument
owns the non-two-central obstruction and the unrestricted I.2.2(5c) assembly.
Source: Aschbacher–Smith I.2.2(5), printed pp.409–412 / PDF pp.420–423.
-/
